PowerVLC: macroblock-level capture hooks for hardware MPEG-2 decoding

Adds the hooks the AppleVA / ATI DVDDriver hardware decoder needs from
libmpeg2 (modules/codec/libmpeg2.c + dvddriver_backend.c):

  - mpeg2_hwaccel_t + mpeg2_hwaccel()   register per-macroblock callbacks
                                        (mb_begin / block / mb_end)
  - mpeg2_set_hw_replace()              skip the CPU IDCT+MC on captured
                                        pictures (replacement mode)
  - mpeg2_pic_field_predicted()         header-level field/frame prediction
                                        signal, reliable even when the
                                        picture is later dropped by sync
  - motion_t.hw_fsel[2]                 field-select bits of the two field
                                        predictions, for the HW descriptors
  - mb_begin gains "mv" and "field_select" arguments

  - mpeg2_hw_rl / mpeg2_hw_rl_n / mpeg2_hw_rl_on / mpeg2_set_hw_rl()
                                        run/level pairs captured during the
                                        VLD itself, so the backend does not
                                        have to rescan the 64 DCTblock
                                        positions per block (PC-sampled at
                                        54 % of mpeg2_slice on the iBook G3)

Until now these lived only as hand edits inside the per-triple contrib
staging directories, so any contrib clean silently reverted the hardware
decoder to a state where modules/codec/libmpeg2.c fails to compile
("unknown type name 'mpeg2_hwaccel_t'").  Keeping them here makes every
contrib prefix reproducible from a clean tree.

The run/level part was still one of those hand edits as of 2026-07-30: the
five legacy prefixes (i686 and the four PowerPC ones) carried it in their
unpacked slice.c while no committed patch did, even though
modules/codec/libmpeg2.c already declares the four symbols extern and calls
them.  It only kept building because the libmpeg2 codec plugin is built for
exactly those slices and not for arm64/x86_64 -- a clean tree, another build
machine, or deleting a .libmpeg2 stamp would all have produced an
undefined-symbol link failure.  Regenerated here from the contrib sources so
the patch reproduces them byte for byte.

--- a/include/mpeg2.h
+++ b/include/mpeg2.h
@@ -153,6 +153,36 @@
 void mpeg2_set_buf (mpeg2dec_t * mpeg2dec, uint8_t * buf[3], void * id);
 void mpeg2_custom_fbuf (mpeg2dec_t * mpeg2dec, int custom_fbuf);
 
+/* PowerVLC : capture pour décodage MPEG-2 accéléré matériel (AppleVA).
+ * Enregistre des callbacks appelés par mpeg2_slice() au niveau macrobloc :
+ *   mb_begin(priv, macroblock_modes, cbp, mv, field_select)  au début du macrobloc
+ *   block(priv, dctblock, scan)            pour CHAQUE bloc codé, dans l'ordre
+ *   mb_end(priv)                           à la fin du macrobloc
+ * cbp est le coded_block_pattern de libmpeg2 (bit 1<<b = bloc b). mv = 8× int16
+ * {MV[fwd][0].xy, MV[bwd][0].xy, MV[fwd][1].xy, MV[bwd][1].xy} en demi-pel (pmv
+ * de libmpeg2, 0 pour l'intra) ; field_select = 4× uint8. Passer hw=NULL (ou des
+ * champs NULL) désactive la capture (décodage CPU normal). */
+typedef struct {
+    void * priv;
+    void (* mb_begin) (void * priv, int macroblock_modes, unsigned cbp,
+                       const int16_t * mv, const uint8_t * field_select);
+    void (* block) (void * priv, const int16_t * dctblock, const uint8_t * scan);
+    void (* mb_end) (void * priv);
+} mpeg2_hwaccel_t;
+void mpeg2_hwaccel (mpeg2dec_t * mpeg2dec, const mpeg2_hwaccel_t * hw);
+/* PowerVLC M4 : active/désactive le mode REMPLACEMENT (saute IDCT+MC CPU sur les
+ * pictures capturées par le GPU → baisse le CPU). Global au décodeur libmpeg2. */
+void mpeg2_set_hw_replace (int on);
+/* PowerVLC 2a (probe-then-commit) : renvoie non nul si la PICTURE COURANTE
+ * (celle dont le header vient d'être parsé, à STATE_PICTURE) utilise la
+ * prédiction/DCT par CHAMP — soit frame_pred_frame_dct=0, soit une field
+ * picture (picture_structure != FRAME). Signal DÉCODÉ AU HEADER, donc fiable
+ * même quand la picture est ensuite DROPPÉE par la synchro (contrairement au
+ * comptage macrobloc field_seen, jamais atteint sur une frame droppée). Sert à
+ * classer progressif vs entrelacé pendant la fenêtre d'observation sans ouvrir
+ * le décodeur HW ni soumettre au GPU. */
+int  mpeg2_pic_field_predicted (mpeg2dec_t * mpeg2dec);
+
 #define MPEG2_ACCEL_X86_MMX 1
 #define MPEG2_ACCEL_X86_3DNOW 2
 #define MPEG2_ACCEL_X86_MMXEXT 4
